{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471338-alaska","id":1471338,"title":"Alaska?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-27T09:07:24-08:00","id":1471338,"title":"Alaska?","content":"So i live in as you guessed it Alaska and i want to run a VTM game here, and i was wondering if there was anything happening here kindred wise? is there any books i could buy that would tell me, like an Alaska by night book or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27244-themastigosequeen","name":"TheMastigoseQueen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27244_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T11:01:43-08:00","id":1471342,"title":"","content":"Sadly no edition of vtm, or other World of Darkness books I know of, have much information on Alaska. This comes down to the environment and population of its cities. The largest of which, Anchorage, is only about 300k strong. A low population like this makes it more likely werewolf books may have something if anything, most likely the tribe known as Wendigo.<br /> <br /> The only thing of note is Alaska's winters are known to have long nights. So you might employ the rules used when vampires stay in the underworld for when the sun isn't active, particularlyfor then staying awake. Both v20, in the Tal'Mahe'Ra book, and v5, in Cults of the Blood Gods, have these rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T11:08:36-08:00","id":1471343,"title":"","content":"There's never been an Alaska focused book, and I'm pretty sure 99% of the WoD material on Alaska is in the WtA books given that one of the Garou Tribes is so focused on the northern parts of North America.<br /> <br /> Alaska is workable, but it's a pretty niche setting for vampires. The largest city in the state has a rather small population by kindred standards, and while tourism is a big deal in Alaska, it isn't as focused on destination cities like NYC, Las Vegas, or New Orleans that have a large consistent tourist population to enable a larger kindred population than the number of permanent residents might imply. Being far enough north to deal with the bouts of minimal or no night/day also puts a large pressure on vampires that want to try to endure that. So crafting a vampire setting in Alaska is going to be a fairly unique process.<br /> <br /> The most helpful book is probably the Dark Ages book that talks about vampire life in Scandinavia, as it has the most talk about how to handle deep winter life for vampires.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T13:04:13-08:00","id":1471349,"title":"","content":"I don't know about anything in VtM's Alaska, but <i>Damnation City</i> includes Anchorage among its two paragraph city examples. It proposes that the community is a small brood of Russian Gangrel. They can't do much in the summer, in spite of the tourists, because of the short nights. They have plenty of time during the winter, but there aren't enough people to feed more than a &quot;handful&quot; of kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T13:18:54-08:00","id":1471350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471338-alaska?p=1471343#post1471343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's never been an Alaska focused book, and I'm pretty sure 99% of the WoD material on Alaska is in the WtA books given that one of the Garou Tribes is so focused on the northern parts of North America.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Even back 25 years ago, I was surprised that Rage Across Alaska wasn't a thing. It would seem to have been the perfect counterpoint to RA New York, in which there's a majority of European tribes and humans in a mostly urban/small town environment next to a sizable chunk of wilderness, verses a place almost entirely wilderness with smaller towns and a few cities, where the majority of the area is dominated by wolf-born and Native Garou. <br /> <br /> For Vampire, its probably a scattering of loners and small groups, mostly among the towns, who probably don't have a whole lot to do with the greater Kindred politics as a whole, save maybe the largest population center or two having a Prince who nominally claims to be for one faction or another, and a few of the local groups being Anarch or Sabbat or whatever. Probably also some transient nomads who drift from place to place or come in and out with shipping traffic. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T17:40:33-08:00","id":1471370,"title":"","content":"I think the prince of Anchorage has been named in a passing reference, but nothing else has been established. Even the name of that prince doesn't pop up on a search of the White Wolf wiki. This just means you have a blank slate to do whatever you want with the location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T21:00:54-08:00","id":1471379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471338-alaska?p=1471350#post1471350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. Even back 25 years ago, I was surprised that Rage Across Alaska wasn't a thing. It would seem to have been the perfect counterpoint to RA New York, in which there's a majority of European tribes and humans in a mostly urban/small town environment next to a sizable chunk of wilderness, verses a place almost entirely wilderness with smaller towns and a few cities, where the majority of the area is dominated by wolf-born and Native Garou.<br /> <br /> For Vampire, its probably a scattering of loners and small groups, mostly among the towns, who probably don't have a whole lot to do with the greater Kindred politics as a whole, save maybe the largest population center or two having a Prince who nominally claims to be for one faction or another, and a few of the local groups being Anarch or Sabbat or whatever. Probably also some transient nomads who drift from place to place or come in and out with shipping traffic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The best that W:tA could manage was the Red Talons entry for Caerns: Places of Power. Their holdings are outside of a <i>Twin Peaks</i>-esque rural town that's haunted by Dancers and fomori. It'd need a bit of work to make the Garou of the sept compatible with actual wolf behavior/not sound like kinky sex stories, since the author was apparently unaware that wolves don't adhere to the Greek letter hierarchy in the wild.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T22:04:25-08:00","id":1471382,"title":"","content":"I can\u2019t think of any other than Caerns: Places of Power for WtA but that sounds like a great idea! I\u2019d love to hear more about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-28T19:30:07-08:00","id":1471414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471338-alaska?p=1471382#post1471382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can\u2019t think of any other than Caerns: Places of Power for WtA but that sounds like a great idea! I\u2019d love to hear more about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As noted, it has a lot of early installment weirdness where the Red Talons are concerned. The captive wolf pack organization is probably the most blatant and jarring given how the tribe grew into being presented later on, with the lack of general bent toward ironically torturing and killing humans in twisted reflections of human religious practices being the runner up (only the Dying Cubs are into that, and they're a shadowy, tiny camp in the smallest tribe). In order to get it up to speed, you'd need to change a lot; the only things you can really take away are that there are Red Talons vaguely close to a rural town and that there are things in town other than grizzly or polar bears that making going out at night a very, very bad idea. You could also keep some or all of the characters, justifying things either way; they could have fallen some time ago and end up replaced by new cubs, or there could be a bunch of isolated near-Elders and Elders that beef up the stats of the younger ones a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-28T19:31:57-08:00","id":1471416,"title":"","content":"I imagine any Vampire campaign set in Anchorage would be a small affair, with a light contingent of Kindred serving as the permanent residents. Interspersed with the occasional transient vampire, Gangrel nomad, migrating character, or folks arriving for special purposes.<br /> <br /> I don't know if Anchorage has the &quot;30 days of night&quot; thing going on, but assuming it does, games would use an irregular structure for games. Protracted periods of activity, where the PCs and NPCs are active for weeks at a time. Followed by similar periods of downtime, where all the vampires hunker down and enter what is effectively a light Torpor during the periods of constant daylight. (A similar arrangement is seen in <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/291774/Magical-Industrial-Revolution\" target=\"_blank\">Magical Industrial Revolution</a>, where all the adventuring in Endon is done during &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Social_season_(United_Kingdom)\" target=\"_blank\">The Season</a>&quot;, followed by months of off-&quot;Season&quot; downtime). Whatever is going on, the Coterie is obliged to get it done while night reigns supreme. It complicates matters in some ways, and simplifies them in others.<br /> <br /> Combine the day-night cycle, the small population (Kindred or Kine), and Alaska's penchant for inclement weather (that can snow in areas), and you have a recipe for a very self-contained, cozy game. Or a batshit insane, claustrophobic fever dream. Whichever.<br /> <br /> Getting Kindred characters out to Anchorage or Alaska as a whole is made easier if the Storyteller invents a good reason for licks to show up. Like a site of magical power or ancient significance, or rumors of the presence of an Elder in Torpor. That kind of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-29T13:21:09-08:00","id":1471452,"title":"","content":"Thank you guys so much, this was all very helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27244-themastigosequeen","name":"TheMastigoseQueen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27244_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-29T17:15:35-08:00","id":1471466,"title":"","content":"If we go by WoD Lore: Sweden is a country where there are night all winter and sun never raise over the horizon.<br /> <br /> But then WOD at that time was written by american writers and most americans dont know that much about the rest of the world (unless US troops have fought a war there <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> So if Sweden by lore is a country where sun never raise over the horizon during winter - then Alaska would have it as dark as if it was hidden in the shadowlands by that time of year. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Now, I live in middle of Sweden and I was out in the sun today with my daughter and build a snow castle in the yard for her, so obviously the Lore does not ring true.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-30T17:55:34-08:00","id":1471514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheMastigoseQueen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471338-alaska#post1471338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So i live in as you guessed it Alaska and i want to run a VTM game here, and i was wondering if there was anything happening here kindred wise? is there any books i could buy that would tell me, like an Alaska by night book or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Please let us know what you do in terms of using Alaska as a setting. I am curious what you do with it. And will you be using Juneau or Anchorage? That is assuming you use either of those cities. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T17:00:35-08:00","id":1471632,"title":"","content":"I look askance at the idea of a &quot;Prince&quot; of Anchorage, unless it's the nominal title of the head of a small brood of associated kindred. The population just won't support enough vampires to have the kind of political intrigues the game assumes as default. And as for a more action-oriented approach, unless the handful of local kindred are all fairly potent elders, one nomadic Sabbat pack passing through or conflict with a single werewolf could wipe out the whole resident population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T00:02:42-08:00","id":1471647,"title":"","content":"The entire state's population isn't really a lot by vampire standards.<br /> <br /> Though the Prince of Anchorage is less absurd if you consider they'd control at least Fairbanks and everything in between, the rest of the Kenai peninsula, and Kodiak island (which is, what ~75% of the state's entire population at that point?). It's very well established in VtM that the Prince of the largest city in an area frequently claims Domain over smaller nearby municipalities rather than their authority ending where humans draw lines on a map. Sure we're still talking about a dozen or so vampires at most.<br /> <br /> And the &quot;appropriate number of vampires&quot; thing is something the books never really cared about. Once you get below the top 20 cities in the US by population, Anchorage is pretty average in size. Either you have to run the setting as only the top 20ish cities in the US have Princes and everywhere else is just a satellite Domain (like Gary Indiana and Santa Monica are actually presented as), or you ignore the numbers in the books to use the dozens of iconic US cities with populations of a few 100K.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T00:43:07-08:00","id":1471650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471338-alaska?p=1471647#post1471647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once you get below the top 20 cities in the US by population, Anchorage is pretty average in size. Either you have to run the setting as only the top 20ish cities in the US have Princes and everywhere else is just a satellite Domain (like Gary Indiana and Santa Monica are actually presented as), or you ignore the numbers in the books to use the dozens of iconic US cities with populations of a few 100K.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even the top 20. Only 11 US cities have a pop of at least 1 million, then 4 more cities are &quot;almost there&quot; in the 900Ks, but all of them still bellow 950K. If you go for city proper while ignoring metro and neighboring areas, then really few cities have enough population for a political body of vampires.<br /> <br /> I don't think even metro area is a good enough measure, although it is surely better. The sparser the population, all the easier for a Prince to claim domain over a larger area and greater the need to do so for administrative and safety reasons, especially in a world where you can get really far with modern transportation.<br /> <br /> As a rule of thumb, you can reasonably consider an area as close enough for interaction purposes if you can get there in less than 3 hours without much of a hassle (outside the hassle of traveling up to 6 hours total), this is enough to make the trip, have some hours to do your business there and be back from sunset to sunrise most of the time in most of the world. Summer can be a hassle depending on where you are, but on those same places winter is a blessing and you can if you set some arrangements to have a safe place to sleep there you can spend the day in your destination and shorten the &quot;lost&quot; time to 3 hours.<br /> <br /> This is not a hard rule on how large a Domain should be, but a starting point of how large an area a single Domain directly influences. The nature and intensity of this influence will depend on many factors. This is also about how far a vampire can live from their feeding grounds on most of the world, so it establishes well how far apart Kindred can live and still be the same &quot;community&quot;, especially if in this area they have no other vampiric communities to be a part of. That's how far a hermit-like vampire can travel to be considered a regular instead of a visitor to the domain, and so forth. For large areas with sparse population this is an extremely useful starting point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T03:26:21-08:00","id":1471651,"title":"","content":"Along with reasoning in terms of metropolitan areas, I also usually take in consideration the number of tourists and the local mobility: travellers and commuters provide for an increased population, which can be sensibly higher than the","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T03:34:25-08:00","id":1471652,"title":"","content":"Of course, the US practically forces you to use metros instead of the strict city limits given the way most states have handled these things. Miami goes from ~450K to over 6 million people when you include its metro, and there's the consideration of 10 to 15 million tourists and travelers that pass through the city most years leaving a large non-resident population instead (Miami is the 44th largest city in the US, but 8th largest metro). But even that doesn't really support how the books present Miami (though being a Sabbat city probably skews that a bit).<br /> <br /> Alaska represents a difficult issue with how far a domain can reasonably go because of the day/night cycle shifts that far north. During the longest days in Anchorage there isn't even six hours of night, and you can't travel north without significant risk as the farther north you go the less night there is. And of course on the other side of it you get the long nights of less than six hours of daylight, when you can go from Anchorage to Fairbanks (~7 hrs by car one way) and still have more than four hours to do things in Fairbanks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T05:41:51-08:00","id":1471654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471338-alaska?p=1471652#post1471652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alaska represents a difficult issue with how far a domain can reasonably go because of the day/night cycle shifts that far north.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't actually think this makes as much of a difference, not in the sense of being a difficult issue. I think it just demands adaptation, but is a pretty reasonable lifestyle.<br /> <br /> Living in such a place, you would take your time during winter to prepare for the shorter nights of summer. Winter's long nights mean you can wander around during parts of the city's day life. It is not only more time to do your stuff, but more access to people and services. This is the ideal time to prepare your things for the summer, which will just require some planning. prepare heavens, learn where the tourists will pass the time, do your more lengthy errands and set up your Summer Hunting Grounds.<br /> <br /> Basically, prepare for Summer in a similar fashion to how mortals in the farmlands prepare for Winter. Make an assessment of what will be your needs and prepare in advance for them, so in the Summer you can spend as little time as possible managing your survival. Summer is a terrible time for long travels, so time your travels to Winter when possible, and so on.<br /> <br /> What I find would be most interesting is to think how those conditions would affect Kindred society. I live in a place where spaces without sun light are exceedingly hard to find, even our basements (that are few) are required by law to have above-ground ceiling and windows, our dumpsters don't have lids and our sewer system is made up of narrow concrete tubes meant to be managed by drilling a hole above ground, there are no tunnels. So when I worked on the WoD version I started to devise a kind of Heaven economy among Kindred, safe places for the day are a precious commodity and some rules, formal and informal, govern ownership, preparation and hospitality.<br /> <br /> So, what would be the social norms the Kindred created to survive and thrive in the far north? How they create new obligations and social expectations, and how they create new opportunities to abuse from your peers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T08:35:12-08:00","id":1471664,"title":"","content":"I don't think the population of whatever city the OP uses actually matters - not in practice. When we actually play the game these numbers (human population v. vampire population) tend to get hand waved away. The coterie will probably be less than a half-dozen people, and with less than a dozen NPCs scattered around. That is enough for a good game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T13:47:11-08:00","id":1471688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471338-alaska?p=1471654#post1471654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't actually think this makes as much of a difference, not in the sense of being a difficult issue. I think it just demands adaptation, but is a pretty reasonable lifestyle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was specifically talking about the difficulties for a Prince attempting to maintain authority over a domain, not how well vampires can adapt to the realities of living that far north. The lifestyle obviously impacts that (one of the reasons I suggested the Prince of Anchorage would lay claim to Kodiak Island, is that it would make a good &quot;summer home&quot; thanks to having more night during the lean times, and a massive cattle industry on an island famous for bears that lets a vampire willing to use cattle for a supplement to human blood disguise their activity easily among the multiple bear attacks on cattle every year).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ....our sewer system is made up of narrow concrete tubes meant to be managed by drilling a hole above ground, there are no tunnels. </div> </div> </div>Just to be clear, sewer tunnels you can actually do much in are basically a myth. A &quot;large&quot; sewer pipe in a major US city is 4 foot vertical (clean, in practice they're smaller as gunk builds up). Fiction generally glosses over the differences between sewers, storm drainage systems (those are generally what gets used as &quot;sewers&quot; because they are larger as their designed to handle sudden surges of water rather than daily use), steam tunnels, underground/subway access and maintenance tunnels, steam tunnels, and buried older city structures that got built over.<br /> <br /> It's fine to include urban myths in the WoD of course, but if you want to keep to a locations unique features, building codes frequently impact that, which means a lot of vampires live in places where their havens need to be above ground, and are probably build more like safe rooms than elaborate sunlight proof basement dwellings (residential requirements for basements with windows is very common).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T17:39:14-08:00","id":1471695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471338-alaska?p=1471688#post1471688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was specifically talking about the difficulties for a Prince attempting to maintain authority over a domain</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where the changes in social norms apply. The Prince may leverage the dynamics of those specific needs to have new avenues for enforcement. For example, lets say a Prince organizes efforts to define an area as Communal Summer Feeding Grounds, and Emergency Heavens around for those who live too far from the area to make the trip there and back in the same night in the height of Summer.<br /> <br /> So this Prince either owns a good chunk of the properties involved and/or coordinate with their owners, and coordinate the efforts to make sure this area will be highly traveled during Summer short nights, probably including as many apartment buildings and hotels as possible as people will be more likely to be at home during the late night hours.<br /> <br /> It doesn't need to be the only available good place to feed, but with so little time of darkness beggars can't be choosers. Everyone knows that things can happen and their personal plans may fail. Everyone knows their survival, or at least well being, may depend on access to this area even if only a couple nights a year. Everyone also knows that messing with things there will mess with the place everyone else relies on.<br /> <br /> Now the Prince has a vital resource that not only makes for leverage, but also encourages the scattered Kindred of the region to show up every now and then, diminishing the impact of their spread through a larger area.<br /> <br /> My point being that the actual ease or difficulty of the Prince will actually depends on how much the Institution of the Prince itself adapted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471338-alaska?p=1471688#post1471688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to be clear, sewer tunnels you can actually do much in are basically a myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Myth with some basis on reality. The problem is that what I described here still applies to all those cases. We don't have service tunnels of any kind for almost anything and even our &quot;subway&quot; is actually mostly above ground, to the point that finding a tunnel deep enough to be dark at day is hard and the subway is basically the only subterranean structure with tunnels more than a meter wide, even our drainage systems use the same concrete tubes of the sewers, not meant to be navigated by humans in any capacity whatsoever.<br /> <br /> To be very clear, I'm aware of the myths about Big Cities sewer systems, but I decided to go with that to enhance the curious difference of my city (this isn't a Brazilian standard, this is Bras\u00edlia, Distrito Federal), and there are other that play on that. But basically speaking, while I am fully aware that actually most Heavens would be normal duelings carefully prepared by their undead inhabitant, the thing is that most cities have some kind of last resort hole a desperate Kindred can try and pray to not be harassed. We have none.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}